<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n34529" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pensātĭo</span></b> ,
			ōnis, f.
		id.. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i>a weighing</i>, <i>weighing out</i>, <i>a
			recompense</i>, <i>compensation</i> (post-Aug.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">multorum bonorum pensatio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Petr. 141, 6</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Dig. 16, 2, 7</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Quint.
				Decl. 2, 32</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Dig. 3, 5,
			7</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, <i>a weighing</i>, <i>pondering</i>, <i>consideration</i>
			(postclass.), <i><span class="en">Amm. 16, 12, 33</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
